%N A401347 Decimal expansion of Product_{k>0} 1/(1 - (2*k)^(-12)).
%H A401347 Aleksandar Petojević, <a href="https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.26039.07847">Exponential Moderateness as a Structural Obstacle in the Theory of Stochastic Very Weak Solutions with Singular Potentials</a>, ResearchGate, 2026. See p. 5.
%F A401347 Equals -Pi^6 * csc(Pi*exp(i*Pi/6)/2) * csc(Pi*exp(5*i*Pi/6)/2) * csch(Pi/2) * sech(sqrt(3)*Pi/2)/32, where i = sqrt(-1).
%F A401347 Equals Pi^6 * csch(Pi/2) * sech(sqrt(3)*Pi/2) / (16*(cosh(Pi/2) - cos(sqrt(3)*Pi/2))). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Oct 22 2026
%e A401347 1.0002442603386002385459471833186990272789973854...
%p A401347 evalf[120](Product(1/(1-(2*k)^(-12)), k=1..infinity));  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 21 2026
%t A401347 RealDigits[Re[-Pi^6 * Csc[Pi*Exp[I*Pi/6]/2] * Csc[Pi*Exp[5*I*Pi/6]/2] * Csch[Pi/2] * Sech[Sqrt[3]*Pi/2]/32],10,100][[1]]
%t A401347 (* Alternative: *)
%t A401347 RealDigits[Pi^6 * Csch[Pi/2] * Sech[Sqrt[3]*Pi/2] / (16*(Cosh[Pi/2] - Cos[Sqrt[3]*Pi/2])), 10, 100][[1]] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Oct 22 2026 *)
